 # RegR 0.1.3
 
+`get_score()` gains a final `metrics = c("AUC", "BS")` argument accepting
+AUC, BS, AIC, BIC and Cox-Snell-type PVE. Selected likelihood criteria share
+the original fit and every Score bootstrap training fit, without extra
+model optimizations; likelihood-only bootstrap reuses `.eff_pblapply()`.
+The original Score fields/class remain available when prediction metrics
+are selected. New `obj`, `AUC.BS.AIC`, individual/combined curve and ROC
+fields carry the corresponding `get_score2()` results; `fit.stats` retains
+numeric likelihood estimates, percentile CIs, resamples and conventions.
+Survival summaries show mean AUC/BS across requested times, with pointwise
+CIs retained in Score and plots. Fine-Gray remains FGR with variance disabled;
+`get_fit_stats()` continues to use mets. `get_score2()` is unchanged.
+
 `get_fit_stats()` computes AIC, BIC and Cox-Snell-type PVE from a shared fit
 for Logistic, Cox and mets Fine-Gray models. Optional percentile bootstrap
 intervals reuse each fitted model across all three statistics and use paired
