+
+When prediction and likelihood metrics are selected together, each Score
+bootstrap training fit supplies all selected likelihood statistics, without
+additional model fitting. AUC/BS evaluate out-of-bag predictions; likelihood
+intervals describe the resampled training fits. With likelihood metrics
+alone, an ordinary paired subject bootstrap uses \code{.eff_pblapply()} with the
+same worker/seed policy as \code{\link[=get_fit_stats]{get_fit_stats()}}.
+
+AIC, BIC and Cox-Snell-type PVE follow \code{\link[=get_fit_stats]{get_fit_stats()}}:
+\code{PVE = 1 - exp(-2 * (LL - LL_null) / n)}. BIC uses subjects for Logistic
+and target events for Cox/Fine-Gray. Fine-Gray uses the FGR/cmprsk likelihood;
+\code{\link[=get_fit_stats]{get_fit_stats()}} uses mets, whose tied-time likelihood can differ. PVE is
+not a Nagelkerke-normalized R-squared. Compare likelihood criteria only
+across models sharing the same outcome, sample and likelihood convention.
+
+Selecting a likelihood metric uses common complete cases across all model
+predictors, time and outcome; omissions are recorded in \code{fit.stats$info}.
+Survival AUC/BS summaries average the requested available times, without
+interpreting variation across times as a confidence interval. Pointwise
+sampling intervals remain in \code{obj$AUC$score} / \code{obj$Brier$score} and plots.
+Logistic summaries use Score's single-point confidence intervals.
+
+Plot fields use ggplot2, optional UtilsR formatting and, for the combined
+survival plot, optional patchwork. Missing patchwork leaves \code{plt.combined}
+as \code{NULL}. Times are used unchanged, without rounding or a fixed axis limit.
